    "chunk_size_bytes": 1698,
    "chunk_text": "Residing in California, Bhikkhuni Tathaloka is a very vital Sangha member of the world group of Buddhist bhikkhunis, known best for helping to establish the Nuns\u2019 Order. It is known that Theravada Buddhist countries like Sri Lanka and Thailand did not have the government nor the leader-monks approve the restarting of the Nuns\u2019 Order. Thailand with a near military government still does not allow women to be ordained. Very fortuitously, Sri Lanka now has a government recognised Meheni Sassnaya. Aided by a monk who was much in the arts, a group of bhikkunis were ordained in India, Buddha Gaya, some years ago. There are several monasteries for these women and they are greatly respected by the people of the area. They are not ten preceptors now; they are fully ordained.\n\nBhikkhuni Tathaloka Theri is a prominent American bhikkhuni known for her part in re-establishing the Nuns\u2019 Order. She has a Monastery near Santa Rosa, CA, offering education, training, and Dhamma teaching. Being a member of the Bhikkhuni Alliance she is involved with the ordination of nuns in North America.\n\nVen Tathaloka Theri has stayed in Sri Lanka more than once. She wanted to telephone me to speak about this article but I was not able do so. Instead she sent much info to my niece who is a student of hers. She lives with her on her trips to the US. The Ven Theri loves Sri Lankan food so my niece cooks for her and cares for her.\n\nEmpowering the next generation: A vision for students\u2019 leadership in Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
