    "chunk_text": "Exclusive academic pathways launched for Sri Lankan aviation professionals\n\nThe Sri Lankan Airlines National Service Union (SLNSS) and the Lincoln Institute of Graduate Studies have announced a strategic partnership to strengthen capacity building across Sri Lanka\u2019s aviation sector.\n\nDriven by a shared vision, the collaboration will provide exclusive educational pathways in Management, Engineering, and Computer Sciences. These tailor-made programs are designed for working professionals, offering flexible study options and industry-relevant learning to enhance qualifications without career interruption.\n\nThe partnership focuses on creating structured academic support and recognised upskilling opportunities, enabling SLNSS members to gain qualifications that contribute directly to career advancement and meet the evolving needs of the industry.\n\nFelix Fernando elected chairman of Joint Apparel Association Forum at 22nd AGM\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
